@startuml invalidation
title Terminal — hover to repaint, one mouse report

skinparam shadowing false
hide footbox

actor User
participant "Terminal" as T
participant "Screen" as S
participant "Container" as C
participant "Button" as B
participant "HoverTracker" as HT

User -> T : moves mouse
T -> T : readSgrMouse()\nESC [ < 35;12;5 M
note right of T
  raw bytes become one
  EventMouseMoved(12, 5)
end note

T -> S : onEvent(EventMouseMoved)

group routing — events travel DOWN
  S -> S : focusables.query({12, 5})
  S -> S : subscriptions & MouseMoved?
  S -> C : onEvent(e)
  C -> C : focusables.query({12, 5})
  C -> HT : set(button)
  HT -> B : setHovered(true)
end

group reaction — the widget changes its own state
  B -> B : onHoverChanged(true)
  B -> B : onEnter()
  note right of B
    state only, no drawing —
    render() is the single place
    that writes to the terminal
  end note
end

group invalidation — travels UP
  B -> C : invalidate(self)
  C -> S : invalidate(self)
  S -> S : dirty.insert(button)
end

note over S
  Still inside one event. Nothing has
  been drawn yet: several events in one
  read burst coalesce into one repaint.
end note

== input burst drained ==

S -> S : if (dirty.empty()) return
S -> B : render(term)
B -> T : underline + "[ + ]"
S -> S : dirty.clear()
T -> User : one flush

note over T, S
  Mode 1003 reports every cell the cursor
  crosses. Without the dirty set that is a
  full clear-and-redraw per cell — the flicker.
  With it, motion inside one widget repaints
  nothing at all.
end note

@enduml
